{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"4a6bc49a56caf02d","type":"text","text":"# **Balance Sheet**\n\nIndicates companies financial position at a specific time, such as end of fiscal year or end of quarter.\n\nAssets = Liabilities + Equity\n\n\n* Assets: resources company controls\n* Liabilities: obligations to lenders\n* Equity: Owner supplied capital\n\nGood way of looking at this is total liabilities plus shareholders equity indicate how all assets are financed either by borrowing from creditors or by equity capital provided by shareholders (They balance).\n\n#### Historical vs Fair value\n\nThis is the way the value of assets are reported. Usually report historical/book value.\n\n* Historical/Book value: cost of acquiring minus any cost expensed to date.\n* Fair value: amount it could be sold for now.\n\nEquity = Assets - Liabilities\n\n* Equity not always same as market value of equity as balance sheet reports book value rather than fair value.","x":-1200,"y":-1000,"width":660,"height":560},
		{"id":"258c8cd45817b3fd","type":"text","text":"# **Assets**\n\nClassified as current or non current, listed in order of liquidity which is how easily can they be converted into cash at fair market value (so cash listed first).\n\n### **Current Assets**\n\n* Cash\n* Inventories\n* Accounts receivable\n\nCurrent assets are expected to be converted to cash, used up or sold within current operating period\n\n* Current operating period: average amount of time elapsed between acquiring inventory and collecting the cash from sales to customers.\n\n### **Non-current Assets**\n\nAlso known as fixed or long term assets\n\n* Land\n* Buildings\n* Machinery\n* Equipment\n* Intangible too like patents\n* ^^ above might be grouped into PP&E\n* Financial assets like bonds\n\n![[Pasted image 20260908085714.png]]\n\n* Similar to the depreciation of tangible assets intangible assets are expensed over their useful lives through amortisation.","x":-1200,"y":-400,"width":660,"height":797,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"05afd80516568b98","type":"text","text":"# **Liabilities**\n\nSplit into current/short term liabilities and long-term debt\n\n### **Current Liabilities**\n\nMust be paid in the next year\n\n* Accounts payable (short term borrowed money and portion of long term debt due within reporting period).\n* Unpaid operating expenses such as money due to workers (shown together as accrued liabilities)\n\n### Long term debt\n\nMoney borrowed repaid over periods longer than one year.","x":-1200,"y":440,"width":730,"height":440,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"6ee29053a2bf43e9","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260908083440.png","x":-200,"y":-1035,"width":693,"height":495},
		{"id":"33ba09abae19d6b1","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260908085555.png","x":-470,"y":-504,"width":755,"height":503},
		{"id":"197a4ddcf4c5ab85","type":"text","text":"# **Equity**\n\nShareholders are the residual owners of the company. They own the residual value of the company after liabilities are paid.\n\nEquity shown in two parts:\n\n* Amount received from selling stocks to common shareholders.\n* Retained earnings/income which represents the companies undistributed income as opposed to dividends which represent distributed income.","x":-438,"y":80,"width":723,"height":800,"color":"#001eff"},
		{"id":"52d4e64835721f22","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260907152726.png","x":-470,"y":-1035,"width":70,"height":70},
		{"id":"f122ad58c450a9b6","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260907152644.png","x":-470,"y":-886,"width":245,"height":198},
		{"id":"59176805e0f611bd","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20260908103704.png","x":560,"y":-1041,"width":646,"height":501},
		{"id":"e1805bd211d4445e","type":"text","text":"## **Conceptual Summary**\n\nTotal liabilities and shareholders equity are how the company assets are financed.\n\nASSETS: What we have\n(Economic resources the company controls to generate profit such as cash, inventory to sell and PP&E)\n\nLIABILITIES + EQUITY: How we paid for it\n(money borrowed and funds provided by the owners of the company)","x":353,"y":-472,"width":853,"height":440,"color":"6"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}